USBuddy downloads third-party components (such as the inference engine and
model weights) at runtime rather than bundling them. Those components are
covered by their own respective licenses, granted directly to the end user
by their upstream providers. See docs/VERIFICATION.md and the signed
artifact manifest for provenance details.

The embedded web chat interface bundles the following open-source
JavaScript libraries (all MIT licensed): React and React DOM (Meta
Platforms, Inc.), Radix UI primitives (WorkOS), zustand (Poimandres),
Lucide icons (Lucide Contributors), clsx (Luke Edwards), and
tailwind-merge (Dany Castillo). Styling is generated with Tailwind CSS
(MIT, Tailwind Labs Inc.).
